{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-5.json\\\")); [print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"],\\\"RULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"],\\\"JUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"],\\\"ITEMS\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"]),\\\"EVIDENCE\\\",json.dumps(list(dict.fromkeys(s.split(\\\"\\\\n    Opinion\\\")[0] for s in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"])))) for x in p]'\"","aggregated_output":"CONTROL 17 RULER How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026? 2027-12-31 JUDGED {'view_id': 'v6', 'question': 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?', 'looks_at': 'Combined data center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers', 'due_day': '2027-02-28', 'year': '2026', 'kind': 'theme'} ITEMS [{\"id\": \"i256\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\", \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\", \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\", \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\", \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\", \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i232\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\", \"passage\": \"2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Alphabet / Google\", \"what\": \"capital expenditure guidance\", \"how_much\": \"up to $190bn\", \"period\": \"2026\", \"status\": \"forecast (guidance)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i233\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\", \"passage\": \"Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Google Cloud\", \"what\": \"revenue growth and backlog\", \"how_much\": \"revenue +63%; backlog nearly doubled to over $460bn\", \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\", \"status\": \"happened\"}}, {\"id\": \"i295\", \"day\": \"2026-07-10\", \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\", \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\", \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\", \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}] EVIDENCE [\"- e45 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan combined data center capital expenditures of around $650 billion in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\", \"- e91 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast hyperscaler spending of $650 billion in calendar 2026 and more than $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\", \"- e162 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author estimates that the four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures .\", \"- e168 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates AI hyperscalers plan $650 billion of data-center capex in calendar 2026 and could spend more than $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\", \"- e389 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the buildout of AI factories was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang put it plainly: \\u201cThe buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\u201d\", \"- e395 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital expenditure guidance to $125\\u2013145 billion.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion\", \"- e403 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Meta Platforms, Microsoft, Alphabet, and Amazon ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Meta, Microsoft, Alphabet, and Amazon are planning higher capital expenditures in calendar 2026; no amounts are given.\\n    Quote: Hyperscalers, including Meta Platforms , Microsoft , Alphabet , and Amazon , are planning higher capital expenditures in 2026.\", \"- e429 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by 247wallst.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\", \"- e457 [fact; ebc.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon recently borrowed another $25 billion, which the article says caused a minor selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"]\nCONTROL 18 RULER How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027? 2028-12-31 JUDGED {'view_id': 'v7', 'question': 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?', 'looks_at': 'Combined data center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers', 'due_day': '2028-02-28', 'year': '2027', 'kind': 'theme'} ITEMS [{\"id\": \"i256\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\", \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\", \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\", \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\", \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\", \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i090\", \"day\": \"2026-07-04\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\", \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\", \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\", \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i143\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\", \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"unnamed estimates\", \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\", \"how_much\": \"about half\", \"period\": \"2027\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i161\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 \\u2014 Is Micron the new Nvidia?\", \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\", \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\", \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\", \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\", \"condition\": \"could reach\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}] EVIDENCE [\"- e46 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers\\u2019 combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\", \"- e91 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast hyperscaler spending of $650 billion in calendar 2026 and more than $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\", \"- e163 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author reports that Nvidia claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\", \"- e168 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source fool.com (Keithen Drury) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates AI hyperscalers plan $650 billion of data-center capex in calendar 2026 and could spend more than $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\", \"- e389 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the buildout of AI factories was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang put it plainly: \\u201cThe buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\u201d\", \"- e429 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by 247wallst.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\", \"- e457 [fact; ebc.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon recently borrowed another $25 billion, which the article says caused a minor selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"]\nCONTROL 19 RULER What Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027? 2027-02-28 JUDGED {'view_id': 'v12', 'question': \"How much revenue will Nvidia's data center segment generate in FY2027?\", 'looks_at': 'Nvidia FY2027 data center segment revenue', 'due_day': '2027-02-28', 'year': 'FY2027', 'kind': 'asset'} ITEMS [{\"id\": \"i129\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"NVIDIA Falls 7% in a Month: Should You Still Hold NVDA Stock or Exit?\", \"passage\": \"During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA reported\", \"what\": \"Q1 FY2027 revenue, data center revenue, non-GAAP EPS\", \"how_much\": \"revenue $81.62B (+85% y/y); data center $75.25B (+92% y/y, +21% q/q, 92% of sales); EPS $1.87\", \"period\": \"Q1 FY2027\", \"status\": \"happened\"}}, {\"id\": \"i281\", \"day\": \"2026-07-09\", \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\", \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA\", \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\", \"how_much\": \"$91 billion \\u00b12%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\", \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\", \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i106\", \"day\": \"2026-07-05\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\", \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\", \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\", \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i208\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\", \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia\\u2019s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street\\u2019s current expectations.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis estimate\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue vs consensus\", \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\", \"period\": \"second half of FY2027\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i295\", \"day\": \"2026-07-10\", \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\", \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\", \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\", \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}] EVIDENCE [\"- e227 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment generated a record $75.2 billion in revenue in FY2027's first quarter.\\n    Quote: its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion\", \"- e241 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] TechCrunch reported that the GPU shortage had eased somewhat by July 2026.\\n    Quote: The GPU shortage that looked so alarming last year has eased off a bit.\", \"- e242 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Russell Brandom said memory-chip makers had increased prices tenfold over the past year as demand outpaced supply growth.\\n    Quote: since demand is growing faster than anyone can scale up supply, they have been able to increase prices tenfold over the past year.\", \"- e243 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Russell Brandom reported that the spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU time peaked at about $3.20 in May 2026 and then steadily declined.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia\\u2019s stock price, there\\u2019s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\", \"- e244 [third_party_view; TechCrunch, Russell Brandom; original source Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Russell Brandom said Google, Amazon, Microsoft and OpenAI had launched custom processors to reduce reliance on Nvidia, and that these chips were good enough to drive down compute prices.\\n    Quote: Google , Amazon , Microsoft , and even OpenAI have launched their own custom processors to lessen their dependence on Nvidia; even if those chips aren\\u2019t as good as the latest model from Nvidia, they\\u2019re good enough to drive down the price of compute.\", \"- e245 [third_party_view; Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch\\u2019s Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said more GPU and accelerator competitors were entering the market, while he expected current market conditions to persist absent a major HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory entrant.\\n    Quote: \\u201cMore GPU and accelerator players are entering the market. Everyone wants to make their own silicon, but no one is making their own DRAM,\\u201d Nelms told me. \\u201cUntil there\\u2019s a major technological breakthrough on HBM [high-bandwidth memory], a shift in supply and demand, or someone new [enters the market in memory], I think things will more or less persist as we see today.\\u201d\", \"- e246 [third_party_view; Citi analyst Atif Malik; original source Citi analyst Atif Malik ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Citi analyst Atif Malik said Nvidia had strong access to DRAM memory amid constrained industry supply.\\n    Quote: We maintain Nvidia as our top buy-rated mega-cap data center semis pick on strong access to DRAM memory amidst constrained industry supply,\", \"- e247 [third_party_view; Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya, in a note this week; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said Nvidia faced gross-margin pressure from higher memory costs, custom-ASIC competition, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing.\\n    Quote: Several concerns are fueling the sell-off, Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya wrote in a note this week. They include gross margin pressure from higher memory costs, competition from custom ASIC chips, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing rather than stronger buybacks/dividends.\", \"- e248 [rumour; barchart.com; original source Unnamed sources cited in reports about DeepSeek ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] DeepSeek is reportedly developing an inference-focused chip and engaging chip-design, foundry, and memory partners while expanding its chip engineering team, potentially reducing reliance on Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Reports that DeepSeek is developing its own inference-focused AI chip could reduce its reliance on Nvidia's GPUs, highlighting a broader industry trend in which leading AI developers are increasingly designing custom silicon to lower costs, improve efficiency, and gain greater control over their AI infrastructure. The project is still in its early stages, with the company engaging chip design, fou\", \"- e249 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] The article says experts see DeepSeek's chip effort as unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, given China's shrinking contribution to sales, but says custom silicon could gradually weaken Nvidia's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\", \"- e251 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia's data center segment revenue set a record in the first quarter; the item gives no amount.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\", \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management guided to accelerating data center segment revenue growth in the second quarter.\\n    Quote: management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\", \"- e262 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects Nvidia will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\", \"- e263 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] QZ says Amazon's Trainium4 chip could arrive later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Amazon 's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\", \"- e264 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta plans three more MTIA generations for generative AI over two years; MTIA 450 is due in early 2027 and MTIA 500 is expected later in 2027.\\n    Quote: Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models. The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory. Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\", \"- e265 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Reuters ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC's Arizona plant and Samsung's Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\", \"- e266 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla is targeting mid-2027 to begin mass production of its AI5 inference chip.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\", \"- e267 [rumour; moomoo.com, citing Reuters and Meta\\u2019s internal memo; original source Meta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, potentially adding competition in AI chips; the year was not specified.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company\\u2019s internal memo.\", \"- e268 [fact; moomoo.com, citing data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta\\u2019s June sales more than doubled year over year to NT$385.19 billion; the company supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia\\u2019s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\", \"- e269 [fact; moomoo.com, citing Bloomberg; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Nvidia server-assembly partner Hon Hai reported June sales up 52% year over year to NT$821.8 billion and quarterly sales up 40%, according to Bloomberg.\\n    Quote: $HON HAI PRECISION INDUSTRY SPON GDS EACH REP 2 SHS TWD10 REG'S' (HNHPF.US)$ , Nvidia\\u2019s server assembly partner, saw a 52% surge in monthly sales in June to NT$ 821.8 billion, allowing the Taiwanese company to post a bigger-than-expected 40% surge in quarterly sales, according to Bloomberg.\", \"- e279 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data showed Nvidia held 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: the company\\u2019s market share has hardly been dented as demand for equipment going into new data centers remains strong. Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\", \"- e286 [fact; Gurufocus, retelling Reuters; original source Meta Platforms ; from gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7 2026-07-10] Meta plans to begin manufacturing its Iris custom AI processor in September, after initial testing; the chip is designed with Broadcom and made by TSMC, and is intended to complement rather than replace Meta's GPU purchases from Nvidia and AMD.\\n    Quote: Reuters said Meta plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing. The chip is being designed with Broadcom (AVGO) and manufactured by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (TSM). The report said the processor is intended to support Meta's AI infrastructure while complementing, rather than replacing, the large number of graphics pro\", \"- e287 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA\\u2019s Q1 FY2027 results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking revenue growth of 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking alone grew 199%.\", \"- e292 [rumour; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] Unnamed reports say major NVIDIA clients, including Meta, are shifting toward developing their own AI chips, raising a potential competitive risk to NVIDIA's Data Center revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's stock surge comes amidst growing concerns that major clients, such as Meta, are shifting towards developing their own AI chips.\", \"- e293 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\", \"- e294 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center Networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier, reflecting surging demand for the Spectrum-X Ethernet and NVLink interconnect systems that travel with every rack-scale Blackwell deployment.\", \"- e296 [rumour; quantumzeitgeist.com; original source Perplexity 2026-07-07; from gnews:b666d35e5247a8ddcc2d7c72 2026-07-10] Perplexity plans to integrate NVIDIA Vera CPUs into its upcoming production systems; no timing or quantity was stated.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now planning to integrate Vera into its upcoming production systems\", \"- e301 [fact; Thomas Richmond, citing NVIDIA\\u2019s report; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\", \"- e303 [fact; TIKR; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported $75 billion in Data Center revenue in its recent quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\", \"- e304 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley said AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of Nvidia\\u2019s demand, indicating demand beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia\\u2019s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\", \"- e326 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com ; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] Nvidia's server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\", \"- e331 [fact; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\", \"- e333 [party_statement; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\", \"- e341 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported Data Center segment revenue of $75.2 billion in its most recent fiscal quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue of $75.2 billion climbed 92%.\", \"- e375 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia's Data Center segment revenue was a record $75 billion in FY2027 Q1, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: The results were driven by record data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92%.\", \"- e377 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom reported Q2 FY2026 AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom\\u2019s Q2 FY2026 revenue hit $22.187 billion, up 47.9%, with AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion growing 143%.\", \"- e378 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan attributed the company\\u2019s sales mix to increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking.\\n    Quote: CEO Hock Tan said the mix is being \\u201cdriven by increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking.\\u201d\", \"- e379 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, and Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion; networking revenue was up 199%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, with Data Center at $75.246 billion and networking alone up 199%.\", \"- e380 [third_party_view; Alex Sirois; original source Alex Sirois 2026-07-13; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] The author said NVIDIA\\u2019s Q2 guidance assumed zero China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA leans on scale and CUDA gravity, but assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue in Q2 guidance, a headwind Broadcom does not carry to the same degree.\", \"- e381 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom management guided to $16.0 billion of AI revenue for Q3, roughly 54% of total sales.\\n    Quote: Broadcom\\u2019s Q3 earnings report lands September 8, and management has already telegraphed $16.0 billion in AI revenue, roughly 54% of total sales.\", \"- e383 [fact; Vandita Jadeja, 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, including Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61 billion, +85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25 billion.\", \"- e384 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA\\u2019s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\", \"- e385 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA\\u2019s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking alone did $14.8 billion, up 199%.\", \"- e387 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing AMD\\u2019s reported results; original source AMD ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] AMD reported $5.775 billion in Data Center revenue in Q1 2026.\\n    Quote: Q1 2026 data center revenue of $5.775 billion.\", \"- e393 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92%, and Networking revenue growth of 199%, for the quarter discussed.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92%, with Networking exploding 199%.\", \"- e398 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Rich Duprey); original source Milk Road AI ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Milk Road AI estimated that one gigawatt of AI infrastructure costs $6\\u201311 billion with Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks, about $19 billion with Nvidia GB300 racks, and $25 billion under Vera Rubin.\\n    Quote: Milk Road AI estimates that building one gigawatt of AI infrastructure using Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks cost between $6 billion and $11 billion, compared with roughly $19 billion using Nvidia GB300-based racks. Under Vera Rubin, rack costs jump to $25 billion.\", \"- e399 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Rich Duprey); original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley\\u2019s forecast, as reported by the author, put the four hyperscalers\\u2019 2027 AI-infrastructure spending above $1 trillion and incremental compute capacity at 19.5 GW; Google was forecast to add 6.8 GW, compared with about 6.7 GW added by the four in 2025.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\", \"- e408 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7 billion.\\n    Quote: For comparison, Nvidia's data center revenue in fiscal 2026 (which ended in January this year) was $193.7 billion.\", \"- e409 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA generated $162.3 billion of fiscal 2026 Data Center revenue from compute chips; the remaining Data Center revenue came from networking components.\\n    Quote: It is worth noting that $162.3 billion of its fiscal 2026 data center revenue came from sales of compute chips, while the rest was from networking components.\", \"- e410 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2026 networking revenue of $31.4 billion, up 142% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company reported a 142% year-over-year increase in networking revenue in fiscal 2026 to $31.4 billion.\", \"- e411 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA's networking revenue tripled year over year to $14.8 billion in the opening quarter of fiscal 2027.\\n    Quote: networking revenue tripling year-over-year to $14.8 billion.\", \"- e419 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA\\u2019s Data Center Networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: with Data Center Networking alone growing 199% YoY to $14.8 billion.\", \"- e421 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Third-party estimates ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Third-party estimates put Nvidia's share of the AI chip market at 80%; the period is not specified.\\n    Quote: The good news is that Nvidia still controls an impressive 80% of the AI chip market, according to third-party estimates.\", \"- e422 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says the shift toward inference and competing chip technologies are weighing on Nvidia's stock performance; the period is 2026.\\n    Quote: The shift from AI training to inference and the emergence of competing chip technologies explain why Nvidia stock has risen just 8% this year despite sustaining impressive growth levels.\", \"- e423 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says inference requires less computing power than training, a shift that could reduce demand for Nvidia's data center products; no period is specified.\\n    Quote: As a result, the inference phase doesn't require as much computing power as the training phase.\", \"- e424 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author estimates Marvell controls 20% to 25% of the custom AI processor market; the period is not specified.\\n    Quote: Marvell is one of the key players in custom AI processors, controlling 20% to 25% of this market.\", \"- e425 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Marvell Technology ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Marvell says it has more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers, with potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion; no completion period is specified.\\n    Quote: In all, Marvell notes that it can tap into more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers in the long run, leading to potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion.\", \"- e428 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA\\u2019s Data Center Networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: with Data Center Networking alone growing 199% on InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\", \"- e433 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: with Data Center alone contributing $75.246 billion (+92% YoY).\", \"- e434 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Networking was the sleeper hit at $14.8 billion (+199% YoY), driven by InfiniBand, Spectrum-X, and NVLink.\", \"- e439 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center segment revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\", \"- e440 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom guided to Q3 revenue of $29.4 billion, up 84% year over year, and stated a goal of exceeding $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 revenue to $29.4B (+84% YoY), and management\\u2019s stated goal is to exceed $100B in AI sales by 2027.\", \"- e441 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom reported AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: AI semi revenue grew 143% YoY to $10.8B last quarter.\", \"- e451 [fact; Tom's Hardware, reporting Reuters; original source U.S. government 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] The U.S. approved ZTE and Maginfra to buy Nvidia H200 chips on July 14, 2026.\\n    Quote: Today, Reuters reports that Chinese telecoms giant ZTE and server firm Maginfra have received U.S. approval to buy Nvidia's last-gen H200 \\\"Hopper\\\" chips.\", \"- e452 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] U.S. policy allows case-by-case sales of Nvidia Hopper-family chips, but not Blackwell chips, to Chinese firms and imposes a 25% export tariff.\\n    Quote: The current status of the AI chip trade situation is roughly that the U.S. allows Chinese firms to buy AI chips up to and including the Hopper family (meaning no Blackwell chips), with a 25% export tariff, though final decisions are made on a case-by-case basis.\", \"- e453 [party_statement; Tom's Hardware, citing CNBC; original source U.S. trade official 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] A U.S. trade official said very few shipments had taken place against licenses for H200 chips and equivalents as of July 14, 2026.\\n    Quote: CNBC cites a U.S. trade official who today stated that \\\"very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It\\u2019s a very small quantity of chips\\\" during a congressional hearing.\", \"- e458 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies a single-node training-server category with one Nvidia HGX B300 eight-GPU assembly and Nvidia BlueField-3 data processing units; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 1 covers single-node training servers built around Intel Xeon 6767P processors with 2-4 TB of RAM, one Nvidia HGX B300 eight-GPU assembly, SSD storage, 25Gb Ethernet, and Nvidia BlueField-3 data processing units for network offload and security [1] .\", \"- e459 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies an integrated rack-scale system category requiring one GB300 NVL72 equivalent with high-speed interconnect, Spectrum-X networking and in-rack cooling; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 2 steps up to integrated rack-scale systems, specifying one GB300 NVL72 equivalent \\u2014 Nvidia's flagship 72-GPU liquid-cooled rack \\u2014 along with high-speed interconnect fabric, Spectrum-X networking architecture, and in-rack cooling [1] .\", \"- e460 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies an AI pod category with performance matching five GB300 NVL72 systems, while allowing Google TPU v8 or v7L or better; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 3 is the most ambitious: an AI pod architecture equivalent to Google TPU v8 or v7L, or better, with performance matching five GB300 NVL72 systems.\", \"- e461 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies Nvidia L40-S accelerators or equivalent for an inference category, with 48GB of GPU memory; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: Category 4 targets inference workloads specifically, calling for Nvidia L40-S accelerators or equivalent with 48GB of GPU memory and support for FP32, FP16, BF16, and INT8 precision formats [1] .\", \"- e462 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in calendar 2026, compared with $675 million in 2024, according to the article.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 \\u2014 a 966% increase.\"]\nCONTROL 20 RULER Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027? 2027-12-31 JUDGED {'view_id': 'v8', 'question': 'Will Nvidia begin shipping its Kyber NVL144 AI server rack by December 31, 2028?', 'looks_at': \"Whether Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 AI server rack begins shipping by the end of 2028.\", 'due_day': '2028-12-31', 'year': '2028', 'kind': 'asset'} ITEMS [{\"id\": \"i100\", \"day\": \"2026-07-05\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\", \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\", \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\", \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\", \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}, {\"id\": \"i179\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\", \"passage\": \"The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"what\": \"four-die Rubin Ultra cancelled; two-die version remains\", \"how_much\": \"roughly half the real-world compute\", \"status\": \"claim\", \"status_note\": \"cancelled\"}}, {\"id\": \"i181\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis, about NVIDIA's plan\", \"what\": \"sell more Oberon-Rubin racks to cover the Kyber gap\", \"status\": \"plan\", \"status_note\": \"as claimed\"}}, {\"id\": \"i101\", \"day\": \"2026-07-05\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\", \"passage\": \"Our roadmap is intact\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA\", \"what\": \"rejects the SemiAnalysis report; says its roadmap (Rubin Ultra / Kyber in 2027) is unchanged\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}, {\"id\": \"i197\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback \\u2014 Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\", \"passage\": \"An Nvidia representative responded with a short statement to Tom's Hardware : \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA representative\", \"what\": \"denies the report: roadmap intact\", \"condition\": \"unclear whether the original or an already updated roadmap is meant\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}] EVIDENCE [\"- e129 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia\\u2019s Kyber NVL144 AI server rack has been delayed more than 12 months to 2028 because its PCB midplane is difficult to manufacture without defects.\\n    Quote: Asian tech stocks slid after analyst firm SemiAnalysis reported on X that Nvidia's next AI server rack system, Kyber NVL144, has been pushed back more than twelve months to 2028 because of manufacturing problems. The issue, according to SemiAnalysis, is the circuit boards. Specifically, the PCB midplane, a central board that connects all the individual components, has proven extremely difficult to\", \"- e139 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia pushed the planned timing for its Kyber rack-scale server design back by more than a year, from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Kyber, Nvidia\\u2019s next rack-scale server design, has been pushed back more than a year , from 2027 to 2028.\", \"- e140 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia\\u2019s eight-rack NVL576 system is likely to be delayed or ship only in small volumes.\\n    Quote: A larger version, called NVL576, which links eight racks together via optical connections, is also likely to be delayed or to ship only in small volumes.\", \"- e141 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that cloud customers rejected Nvidia\\u2019s plan to bolt two current-generation racks together, citing awkward design and high operating costs.\\n    Quote: Cloud customers reportedly rejected it because the design was awkward and the service was expensive to run.\", \"- e160 [rumour; CNBC.com; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:b48593184704bbbe6eddbc03 2026-07-07] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia was at least a year behind on manufacturing its next line of server racks.\\n    Quote: a research report claiming the AI leader was at least a year behind on manufacturing of its next line of server racks\", \"- e161 [party_statement; CNBC.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:b48593184704bbbe6eddbc03 2026-07-07] Nvidia disputed SemiAnalysis's report that its next-generation Kyber server rack was running into delays.\\n    Quote: the company disputed a report by SemiAnalysis that its next-gen Kyber server rack was running into delays\", \"- e170 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA\\u2019s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale AI system had been delayed from its planned 2027 launch to 2028.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis reported on July 5\\u20136, 2026 that NVIDIA\\u2019s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale AI system has been delayed, from its planned 2027 launch to 2028.\", \"- e171 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA spokesperson 2026-07-06; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remained intact, disputing the report that Kyber NVL144 had been delayed to 2028.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA publicly disputed the report on Monday, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg its \\u201croadmap is intact.\\u201d\", \"- e172 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA\\u2019s NVL576 rack-scale system was also likely to be delayed or limited to small initial volumes.\\n    Quote: A larger sibling, the NVL576, designed to link eight racks via optical connections, is also likely delayed or limited to small initial volumes, according to SemiAnalysis.\", \"- e174 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Lisa Su ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] AMD CEO Lisa Su said customer engagement for the MI450 Series and Helios was strengthening, and leading-customer forecasts exceeded AMD\\u2019s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: CEO Lisa Su has said \\u201ccustomer engagement around MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations.\\u201d\", \"- e210 [third_party_view; futuriom.com, relaying SemiAnalysis\\u2019s X post; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] SemiAnalysis said in an X post that NVIDIA\\u2019s Kyber NVL144 rack system had hit manufacturing setbacks.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s stock also suffered this week because research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA\\u2019s Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks\\u2014a situation that could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model, creating a continuing flow of demand for its products.\", \"- e211 [party_statement; futuriom.com, quoting an NVIDIA spokesperson; original source NVIDIA spokesperson ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] An NVIDIA spokesperson said the company\\u2019s product road map remained intact.\\n    Quote: An NVIDIA spokesperson said, \\u201cOur road map is intact.\\u201d\", \"- e212 [party_statement; futuriom.com, quoting an NVIDIA spokesperson; original source NVIDIA spokesperson ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] An NVIDIA spokesperson said Vera Rubin Ultra was planned to scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in 2027.\\n    Quote: Further, \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline.\\\"\", \"- e260 [fact; IEEE Spectrum; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:a4eb2bdfabca94f5887881c6 2026-07-09] Nvidia plans to increase the number of GPUs in a single interconnected system from 72 to as many as 576 by 2027.\\n    Quote: At the same time, Nvidia is planning to add even more processors to single interconnected systems, going from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 by 2027.\", \"- e305 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] NVIDIA denied reports that the Kyber platform is being delayed.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) has denied reports that the Kyber platform is being delayed.\", \"- e306 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer; original source Semi Analysis ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] Semi Analysis said everything could be late for NVIDIA because one part of its business is late.\\n    Quote: Semi Analysis does pretty good work, saying that everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late.\", \"- e344 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of manufacturing trouble with a crucial circuit board.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\", \"- e345 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Nvidia said its product roadmap, including the Kyber NVL144 schedule, remains intact.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact, although questions linger.\", \"- e346 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Geoffrey Seiler 2026-07-12; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] The author said AMD's ROCm improvements and programmers' use of open-source frameworks such as OpenAI's Triton have narrowed AMD's software ecosystem gap with Nvidia, especially for inference.\\n    Quote: AMD has greatly improved its ROCm platform over the past few years, and the move of programmers working higher up the software stack and using open-source AI frameworks like OpenAI's Triton have helped close the gap, especially for inference.\", \"- e347 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Geoffrey Seiler 2026-07-12; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] The author said AMD's chiplet designs and recent acquisition of memory optimization software platform Mext position it to offer a high-end server solution designed for inference.\\n    Quote: AMD's chiplet designs, which can package more memory onto its chips, and its recent acquisition of memory optimization software platform Mext, position it well to offer a high-end server solution designed specifically for inference.\", \"- e348 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Geoffrey Seiler 2026-07-12; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] The author said a Kyber delay could make Alphabet's cost-efficient TPU offering more attractive to customers seeking an optimized system without Nvidia-platform delay risk or premium cost.\\n    Quote: A delay in Kyber, meanwhile, could make its cost-efficient TPU offering look more attractive to customers that want a completely optimized system without the risk of delay or the cost of Nvidia's premium platform.\", \"- e454 [rumour; ebc.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] SemiAnalysis reportedly said over the weekend that Nvidia\\u2019s Kyber NVL144 architecture could be delayed into 2028.\\n    Quote: Over the weekend, reports circulated from industry research firm SemiAnalysis suggesting that Nvidia\\u2019s upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028.\", \"- e455 [party_statement; ebc.com; original source Nvidia spokesperson ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] An Nvidia spokesperson said the company\\u2019s roadmap remained intact, countering reports of a Kyber NVL144 delay.\\n    Quote: Although an Nvidia spokesperson quickly countered the reports, telling that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\"\"]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-5.json\\\")); x=p[2]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(dict.fromkeys(s.split(\\\"\\\\n    Opinion\\\")[0] for s in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"] if any(t in s.lower() for t in [\\\"91 billion\\\",\\\"20% above\\\",\\\"100 billion\\\",\\\"100 bn\\\",\\\"75.25\\\",\\\"75.2 billion\\\"]))))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-5.json\\\")); x=p[2]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(dict.fromkeys(s.split(\\\"\\\\n    Opinion\\\")[0] for s in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"] if any(t in s.lower() for t in [\\\"91 billion\\\",\\\"20% above\\\",\\\"100 billion\\\",\\\"100 bn\\\",\\\"75.25\\\",\\\"75.2 billion\\\"]))))'\"","aggregated_output":"- e227 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment generated a record $75.2 billion in revenue in FY2027's first quarter.\n    Quote: its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion\n- e293 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\n- e301 [fact; Thomas Richmond, citing NVIDIA’s report; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\n- e331 [fact; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\n- e333 [party_statement; barchart.com (author); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia guided to approximately $91 billion in Q2 FY2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\n- e341 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported Data Center segment revenue of $75.2 billion in its most recent fiscal quarter, up 92% year over year.\n    Quote: Data center revenue of $75.2 billion climbed 92%.\n- e383 [fact; Vandita Jadeja, 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, including Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61 billion, +85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25 billion.\n- e439 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center segment revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92% year over year.\n    Quote: Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\n- e440 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] Broadcom guided to Q3 revenue of $29.4 billion, up 84% year over year, and stated a goal of exceeding $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 revenue to $29.4B (+84% YoY), and management’s stated goal is to exceed $100B in AI sales by 2027.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-5.json\\\")); x=p[2]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(dict.fromkeys(s.split(\\\"\\\\n    Opinion\\\")[0] for s in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"] if any(t in s.lower() for t in [\\\"consensus\\\",\\\"semianalysis\\\",\\\"margin\\\",\\\"accelerat\\\",\\\"quarter mark\\\",\\\"100bn\\\",\\\"100 bn\\\"]))))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-5.json\\\")); x=p[2]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(dict.fromkeys(s.split(\\\"\\\\n    Opinion\\\")[0] for s in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"] if any(t in s.lower() for t in [\\\"consensus\\\",\\\"semianalysis\\\",\\\"margin\\\",\\\"accelerat\\\",\\\"quarter mark\\\",\\\"100bn\\\",\\\"100 bn\\\"]))))'\"","aggregated_output":"- e245 [third_party_view; Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch’s Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said more GPU and accelerator competitors were entering the market, while he expected current market conditions to persist absent a major HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory entrant.\n    Quote: “More GPU and accelerator players are entering the market. Everyone wants to make their own silicon, but no one is making their own DRAM,” Nelms told me. “Until there’s a major technological breakthrough on HBM [high-bandwidth memory], a shift in supply and demand, or someone new [enters the market in memory], I think things will more or less persist as we see today.”\n- e247 [third_party_view; Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya, in a note this week; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said Nvidia faced gross-margin pressure from higher memory costs, custom-ASIC competition, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing.\n    Quote: Several concerns are fueling the sell-off, Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya wrote in a note this week. They include gross margin pressure from higher memory costs, competition from custom ASIC chips, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing rather than stronger buybacks/dividends.\n- e249 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] The article says experts see DeepSeek's chip effort as unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, given China's shrinking contribution to sales, but says custom silicon could gradually weaken Nvidia's pricing power and margins.\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\n- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management guided to accelerating data center segment revenue growth in the second quarter.\n    Quote: management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\n- e378 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan attributed the company’s sales mix to increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking.\n    Quote: CEO Hock Tan said the mix is being “driven by increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking.”\n- e461 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI's RFI specifies Nvidia L40-S accelerators or equivalent for an inference category, with 48GB of GPU memory; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\n    Quote: Category 4 targets inference workloads specifically, calling for Nvidia L40-S accelerators or equivalent with 48GB of GPU memory and support for FP32, FP16, BF16, and INT8 precision formats [1] .\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"control\":17,\"same_question\":\"yes\",\"same_due\":\"yes\",\"items\":{\"i256\":\"shown\",\"i232\":\"not_shown\",\"i233\":\"not_shown\",\"i295\":\"not_shown\"},\"why\":\"The evidence does not show Alphabet's $190 billion capex guidance, Google Cloud's 63% revenue growth and over $460 billion backlog, or NVIDIA's accelerating growth as quarterly revenue approaches $100 billion.\"}\n{\"control\":18,\"same_question\":\"no\",\"same_due\":\"yes\",\"items\":{\"i256\":\"shown\",\"i090\":\"not_shown\",\"i143\":\"not_shown\",\"i161\":\"not_shown\"},\"why\":\"The judged question limits spending to four hyperscalers while the ruler does not specify four, and the evidence omits the 82% and 41% revenue growth forecasts, memory's estimated half of 2027 data-center spending, and Goldman Sachs's AI infrastructure spending estimates.\"}\n{\"control\":19,\"same_question\":\"yes\",\"same_due\":\"yes\",\"items\":{\"i129\":\"shown\",\"i281\":\"shown\",\"i106\":\"not_shown\",\"i208\":\"not_shown\",\"i295\":\"not_shown\"},\"why\":\"The evidence omits SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half FY2027 data-center compute revenue would be 20% above consensus and NVIDIA's claim of accelerating growth as quarterly revenue approaches $100 billion.\"}\n{\"control\":20,\"same_question\":\"no\",\"same_due\":\"no\",\"items\":{\"i100\":\"shown\",\"i179\":\"not_shown\",\"i181\":\"not_shown\",\"i101\":\"shown\",\"i197\":\"shown\"},\"why\":\"The judged question asks about shipping by the end of 2028 rather than 2027, and the evidence omits the claimed cancellation of the four-die Rubin Ultra and the plan to sell more Oberon-Rubin racks.\"}"}}
